NNAAMMEE
     aaccccttoonn — enable/disable system accounting

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     aaccccttoonn [_a_c_c_t_f_i_l_e]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aaccccttoonn utility is used for switching system accounting on or off.  If
     called with the argument _a_c_c_t_f_i_l_e, system accounting is enabled.  The
     _a_c_c_t_f_i_l_e specified must exist prior to starting system accounting, or
     aaccccttoonn will return an error.  A record of every process that is started
     by the execve(2) system call and then later exits the system is stored in
     _a_c_c_t_f_i_l_e.  The sa(8) command may be used to examine the accounting
     records.  If no arguments are given, system accounting is disabled.

FFIILLEESS
     /var/account/acct  default accounting file

